    "body": "<!-- markdownlint-disable -->\n\n## Overview\n\nAdd `GPUModelRunner.override_model_forward(fn)` (MRV2): a context manager under which `execute_model` still builds the step's inputs, attention metadata and forward context, then calls `fn(input_batch, **model_inputs)` instead of the eager model call. Its user is `vllm bench forward` (#61339, stacked on this PR), which times the model forward of an exact batch as a one-shot CUDA graph.\n\n## Claims\n\n- A benchmark can run the real per-step preparation (input batch, `ModelState` metadata, DP sync, forward context) for a batch it built, and take over only the model call, without copying runner code or patching private state.\n- No behavior change unless the context manager is active: one attribute check in the eager branch.\n\n## Validation\n\nExercised by the stacked bench PR's tests (`tests/benchmarks/test_forward_cli.py`, end-to-end on Llama-3.2-1B in the Benchmarks CLI job) and its validation on DeepSeek-V4/V4.1 (1 to 8 GPUs, DP/TP/EP, 2 nodes). The hook alone has no caller in this PR, so it has no separate test.\n\n## Details\n\n- Only the eager branch (`cudagraph_mode == NONE`, no micro-batching) is overridable; the context manager asserts both, since otherwise the override would never reach the model.\n- `fn` receives the `InputBatch` so a caller can check the layout the runner built (request order, query and computed lengths) and write per-request inputs, without reading runner internals.\n- `sample_tokens` must not follow an overridden step, so the pending `execute_model_state` is dropped on exit.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensur